Shift-cut forward test: two models it called 100% infeasible run correctly on the DPU
2026-09-09. Desktop 2 (Phoenix, Ryzen 7 8700G), resnet_env17, Ryzen AI 1.7.1,
phoenix/4x4.xclbin. These runs DID take a hardware context, one at a time, each on a fresh
compile cache. `xrt-smi examine -r aie-partitions` reported "No hardware contexts running on
device" beforehand and tools/host_load.ps1 reported HOST_LOAD_VERDICT CLEAR at 0.34 busy
cores of 16 -- the quietest the machine has been all sitting.

THIS IS THE SECOND HALF OF AN EXPERIMENT. The predictions were fixed and committed before any
of these ran, in results/quant/shift_cut_forward_predictions.log. Nothing below was selected
after the fact; the models run are the two the prediction log named in advance, plus a
same-architecture-class control and a well-placing detection model.

Commands (from the repo root, resnet_env17, RYZEN_AI_INSTALLATION_PATH set):
  python tools/shift_cut_forward_test.py models/<model>.onnx --cache-key <key> \
      --input-range {byte,unit} [--image data/calib/000000.jpg]

