--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. READING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  model                        prediction    NPU nodes   corr vs CPU   max/peak
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sesr_m7_fp32_xint8           HAZARD 9/9      50 / 52      0.99912      0.040
  sesr_m7_nchw_xint8           HAZARD 9/9      50 / 52      0.99913      0.041
  test_sr_xint8                clean  0/2       8 / 17      1.00000      0.008
  yolov8n_cut_xint8_c32        clean  0/177   922 / 929   0.880-0.979    <=0.543

THE BOLDEST PREDICTION IS REFUTED, TWICE. Both SESR artifacts were called infeasible on
every one of their nine operations. Both place 50 of 52 nodes on the NPU -- the two that do
not are a QuantizeLinear/DequantizeLinear pair, not compute -- and both track their own CPU
reference at a correlation of 0.999 with a worst-case deviation of 4% of peak on a smooth
pixel mapping. That is ordinary requantization divergence. It is not what a model whose
requantizer cannot represent its scales looks like; for comparison, the failure this
predictor is meant to catch took BiSeNetV2 from 59.47% pixel accuracy under CPU simulation to
15.33% on hardware.

AND A THIRD CASE WAS ALREADY IN THE PREDICTOR'S OWN EVIDENCE. results/quant/shift_cut_
feasibility.log, on branch `main`, shows sesr_m7_xint8.onnx at 9 of 9 violations. That
artifact's measured NPU quality is 34.06 dB PSNR on Set5 against a 35.64 dB float reference,
and 35.16 dB with AdaRound (docs/BENCHMARKS.md, results/eval_sesr_m7_set5_npu.log). So three
SESR artifacts are called 100% hardware-infeasible and all three work. The rule fires on the
whole architecture family.

THE CLEAN DIRECTION IS NOT SETTLED BY THIS RUN, AND THE METRIC IS WHY. test_sr_xint8 agrees
to a correlation of 1.00000, but only 8 of its 17 nodes reach the NPU, so it exercises little
of the DPU. yolov8n_cut_xint8_c32 places 922 of 929 and still shows correlations from 0.880
to 0.979 on its raw head tensors -- yet this repo's own known-good yolov8n-cut reports
BYTE-IDENTICAL decoded detections between CPU and NPU. Raw-tensor correlation is therefore
too sensitive for a detection head: it moves for reasons that never reach the task output.
The metric is sound for super-resolution, where the tensor IS the output, and that is exactly
where the decisive result sits.

WHAT THIS MEANS FOR IGNITION. The shift-cut audit must not gate Ignition in its current form.
A rule that calls an entire working architecture family 100% infeasible would reject good
artifacts, and rejecting good work silently is worse than missing bad work. What the audit
may still be doing correctly is a separate question this does not answer: its BiSeNetV2 and
RegNetX-002 flags coincide with real, documented hardware failures, and nothing here disturbs
those. The honest summary is that it has one confirmed false-positive mode, of the widest
possible kind, and its true-positive claims remain retrodictive.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- It does not show the shift-cut bound is wrong as physics. The 15-bit multiplier and the
  sigma in [0, 31] window are read from the hardware's requantizer. What is shown wrong is
  the classifier built on top of them, on this family.
- It does not test the audit's positive claims on BiSeNetV2 or RegNetX-002. Those remain
  consistent with their known failures and untested forward.
- Agreement is measured on one seeded input per model, and on one real image for the
  detection model. It is an output-agreement probe, not a dataset evaluation.
- realesrgan_compact_r64_xint8 was in the prediction set and is NOT reported as a result: its
  first run fed a 0-255 input to a model that npu/realesrgan.py scales to 0-1, which
  saturates both paths and makes the comparison meaningless, and it places only 12 of 248
  nodes on the NPU. It is a poor vehicle and the invalid run is discarded rather than quoted.
- Every remaining model in the prediction set is still unrun. The predictions stand as
  recorded.
